A region taken from a process another core runs is marked to be loaded again, but that core is not made to trap.
Its protection unit keeps the region while its thread runs on, so the memory could become a pool the thread still reaches;
a core runs user mode only with the regions its thread's process has.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2 smp-test
Report: a core runs user mode with regions its process no longer has

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -133,7 +133,6 @@ void core_regions_changed(const struct process *proc)
         struct core *c = &cores[i];
         if (c != core_self() && c->current != NULL && thread_process(c->current) == proc) {
             c->pmp_stale = true;
-            core_shoot(c);
         }
     }
 #else
